          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Bolivia imports 60% of wheat, 86% of diesel, significant medicine. Depends on neighbors' ports.
            The Yungas is partially buffered by local food production but would lose access to fuel,
            medicine, and staples.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-800/50 border border-bark-700 rounded-xl p-8 reveal" data-delay="300">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-50 text-sm">Global Financial Crisis</h3>
            <span class="font-display font-bold text-ember text-2xl">3/10</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Bolivia is already in a financial crisis. A global one layered on top would be catastrophic.
            Reserves near zero. Currency in freefall. Rural subsistence communities would fare better
            than urban populations, but that is cold comfort.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-800/50 border border-bark-700 rounded-xl p-8 reveal" data-delay="350">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-50 text-sm">Pandemic / Biological Crisis</h3>
            <span class="font-display font-bold text-ember text-2xl">3/10</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Healthcare system is genuinely weak. COVID-19 killed at 7x normal rates in poorest departments.
            The Yungas has no hospital infrastructure. Rural isolation provides some disease-spread protection
            but zero treatment capacity.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-800/50 border border-bark-700 rounded-xl p-8 reveal" data-delay="400">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-50 text-sm">Composite Assessment</h3>
            <span class="font-display font-bold text-bark-300 text-lg">Context-dependent</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Excellent for nuclear scenarios. Mediocre to poor for everything else.
            The honest answer is that it depends on which crisis you are preparing for.
            A community that builds its own resilience changes the equation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
